WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:05.389
Monday, 11:20 AM. Lecture ran over. You're 30 minutes behind, and your shift starts at 2.

2
00:00:07.559 --> 00:00:13.430
TimeWise is a free planner for students whose weeks don't go as planned.

3
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.603
Start by adding your week. Connect Google Calendar, import a calendar file, or type your classes.
Setup takes about five minutes.

4
00:00:17.907 --> 00:00:22.231
Start by adding your week. Connect Google Calendar, import a calendar file, or type your classes.
Google will warn the app isn't verified. Click Advanced, then Go to TimeWise. It's read-only.

5
00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:33.206
Or type your classes. It takes about a minute.

6
00:00:33.511 --> 00:00:35.213
Here's a full week, using Maya's sample week.

7
00:00:35.263 --> 00:00:43.600
Each morning, Today shows what's next, how much free time you have left, and what needs attention.

8
00:00:43.906 --> 00:00:48.879
Running behind? Tell TimeWise what changed.

9
00:00:49.184 --> 00:01:00.153
Classes and shifts stay put. Everything else shifts, and whatever won't fit moves to tomorrow.

10
00:01:00.459 --> 00:01:08.794
Missed something? That's fine. Put it back in one tap.

11
00:01:09.099 --> 00:01:19.878
At night, mark what happened. You get one pattern and one small change for tomorrow. No score.

12
00:01:20.536 --> 00:01:25.000
Start my week at timewise.aydink.workers.dev. Sign in with Google so it saves.
